# contests.dat - contest definitions for ShackBook (#4)
#
# What a contest IS: its exchange, and whether it is a county-based state
# party. Enough to lay out an entry form, drive a worked/needed table, and
# sanity-check a Cabrillo export. NOT a scoring model - multipliers and
# points rules are deliberately out of scope, see src/ContestDef.h.
#
# Format, one record per line, pipe-separated:
#   ID|Name|SentFields|ReceivedFields|CountyState|OutOfState|Status
#
# ID              Cabrillo CONTEST: value, uppercase; matches qsos.contest_id
# SentFields      comma-separated, IN SENDING ORDER - this sets tab order
# ReceivedFields  same, for what the other station sends
# CountyState     two-letter state whose counties are the multiplier; empty
#                 for contests that are not county-based
# OutOfState      1 when out-of-state stations also work each other, else 0
# Status          CONFIRMED or UNCONFIRMED - see below. Required.
#
# Field names: RST, SERIAL, COUNTY, STATE, SECTION, GRID, NAME, POWER, AGE,
#              TEXT
#
# -- THE STATUS COLUMN, and why it is per-row -----------------------------
#
# A definition that is present but WRONG is worse than one that is absent,
# because the entry form and the Cabrillo check would both act on it. So
# every row states its own provenance, rather than relying on a note at the
# top of the file that whoever edits one row will never read.
#
#   CONFIRMED    the exchange has been checked against the sponsor's own
#                published rules, with the year checked in a comment above
#                the row. Safe to drive a submitted log.
#
#   UNCONFIRMED  the exchange is the COMMON county-party shape (RST +
#                county, some with a serial) and is probably right, but
#                nobody has read the sponsor's rules to verify it. Usable
#                for a worked/needed table, where being wrong costs a
#                mis-labelled column. NOT to be trusted for a submitted log
#                until someone confirms it.
#
# EVERY ROW BELOW IS CURRENTLY UNCONFIRMED. That is honest rather than lazy:
# these shapes were written from general knowledge of how state parties
# work, not from the rules. Rules also change between years, which is why
# even a CONFIRMED row has to carry the year it was confirmed.
#
# To confirm a row: read the sponsor's current rules, correct the exchange
# if needed, change UNCONFIRMED to CONFIRMED, and add a comment above it
# naming the source and year. Treat any mismatch found in use as a bug in
# THIS FILE, not in the code that reads it.
#
# Blank lines and lines beginning with # are ignored.
#
MDC-QSO-PARTY|Maryland-DC QSO Party|RST,COUNTY|RST,COUNTY|MD|0|UNCONFIRMED
FLQP|Florida QSO Party|RST,COUNTY|RST,COUNTY|FL|0|UNCONFIRMED
CQP|California QSO Party|RST,SERIAL,COUNTY|RST,SERIAL,COUNTY|CA|0|UNCONFIRMED
PAQP|Pennsylvania QSO Party|RST,SERIAL,COUNTY|RST,SERIAL,COUNTY|PA|0|UNCONFIRMED
OHQP|Ohio QSO Party|RST,COUNTY|RST,COUNTY|OH|0|UNCONFIRMED
TXQP|Texas QSO Party|RST,COUNTY|RST,COUNTY|TX|0|UNCONFIRMED
